Hello OMG! Ubuntu team,

an app tip for the Linux desktop, with the details your readers usually ask
for first.

Solidon3D is a desktop application for editing downloaded 3D models without
CAD knowledge — move a hole in a printable part, change a countersink, add a
thread that fits. It ships as a Flatpak and an AppImage for Linux, alongside
Windows and macOS builds. One-time purchase, no subscription. After a single
activation it runs fully offline: no account, no telemetry, no server
requirement. A machine with no network connection can be activated via a file
and a second device.

Version 0.5.0 is a large step. Until now an edited model came back out as a
triangle mesh; now it is an exact body with real faces and edges, and holes,
slots, countersinks, bosses, beads, grooves and threads stay exact when they
are moved, duplicated, rotated or removed. STEP goes in and comes back out
cleanly, so the result can be carried into FreeCAD or any other CAD tool.

The most immediately visible change: a honeycomb pattern, a knurl or a set of
ribs is recognised as one feature with pitch, cell width and depth instead of
hundreds of faces, and can be removed with a click or reapplied with three
numbers — including around a cylindrical handle.

Two more that matter in daily use: dimensions are edited on the model itself
with a live preview, and the application starts in half the time it used to.

There is an assistant with AI features. It is optional, can be switched off
entirely, and can run locally on your own GPU — nothing is required to leave
the machine.

70 user-visible changes in this release; 896 since the first 0.1 demo.
Interface and manual in six languages. A demo is available.

Solidon3D is a desktop application for Windows, macOS and Linux. One-time
purchase, no subscription, no account: after a single activation it runs fully
offline. Interface and manual are available in six languages, and there is a
demo.

I am happy to provide a review licence, print-resolution images or answers to
any question directly.

